ARK is all around a fun and enjoyable game. Official servers are extremly grindy, but Unofficial are usually on point. There are tons of mods that will keep you playing the game for hours on hours. The community is OK, usually on unofficial you will find more players that will assist you, rather than not.
HOWEVER;
The game is HORRIBLY optimized, you basically need 450 1080ti's to run this at a decent frame rate on Medium settings. And now that they've bumped the price to $60, and wanting you pay an additional $19.99 for Scorched is absolutely inane. It's also very buggy. Your dinos will fall through the ground, you'll walk through mountains, items randomly disappear, dinos overspawn, and more..

